From 4041ca7f4d0ec3882194b5f2937bf0174e4c5e58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unrent <76983160+boostings@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:24:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pad): generic motion pad controller for Unreal-hosted
 motion games

New motion games hosted by the Movecade Kart PC game (sumo, derby, fishing)
have no web canvas and no bespoke phone screen. They get one generic phone
controller, the motion pad, and the room server accepts their ids.

Protocol (protocol/src/motionPad.ts): MOTION_PAD_GAMES is the one list.
An entry makes the id a known room game (normalizeGameId, the host
handshake, configure-room), puts it in the free / premium / simultaneous
lists and the score ceilings, lets a phone calibrate for it
(isMotionGame, its own grip text), and maps it to the pad on the phone.
The web catalog stays as it is, so these games stay out of the web
picker, SEO, leaderboards, iOS and Go catalogs.
- sumo and fishing are simultaneous; derby is turn-based (one batter at a
  time, named with advance-turn like bowling).
- All three are premium, like every game but bowling. Premium gates
  nothing unless ENABLE_MONETIZATION=true, which local dev and current
  production leave off.
- pad:prompt is host-only (HOST_ONLY_GAME_EVENTS).

Phone (app/src/games/pad): findGame falls back to the pad plugins. The
pad shows the host's pad:prompt for this player (or "*") big, one or two
big buttons sending pad:press / pad:release {button} on pointer down /
up with a buzz (keyboard too, released on hide, unmount, or a button the
host removes), and a per-mode hint animation (tilt, swing, aim, flick)
that respects reduced motion. The shell streams calibrated frames at
the game's sendHz (100 Hz for swings and flicks, 60 for tilt) while
active, as for samurai. Prompts are collected from the moment the room
is a pad room, so one that lands just before the turn flips is shown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
